{"agent":"i1-kilo","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`ddflow.adapters.mcp_client` imports several names from `.mcp` (`CLOSED_BEFORE_READ`, `ECHOED`, `EOF`, `ERROR`, `OFFER_VERSION`, `OK`, `POLL_S`, `TIMEOUT`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `Negotiation`, `describe_answer`, `encode`, `initialize_request`, `negotiate`, `request`, `response_in`), but `ddflow.adapters.mcp` is being split and reduced in size. If `ddflow.adapters.mcp` no longer exports these names or if `ddflow.adapters.mcp` itself needs to import items from `mcp_client`, this will create a circular import at runtime when any module imports `ddflow.adapters.mcp` (which re-exports everything from `mcp_client` according to the module docstring). Given that `mcp` imports nothing from `mcp_client` in the provided diff while `mcp_client` imports from `mcp`, any attempt by `mcp` to re-export `McpClient`, `StdioClient`, or related types defined in `mcp_client.py` will fail due to a circular import when `mcp` is imported before `mcp_client` is fully initialized, or will raise an `ImportError` if those names are not explicitly re-exported in `ddflow/adapters/mcp.py` (which is not shown as modified to add re-exports).","digest":"c3823d291649c65b","family":"google","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:41","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:41"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The move deletes the public helper `send_line` from `ddflow.adapters.mcp` and the re-export list does not bring it back (only `Channel`, `Handshake`, `McpClient`, `Outcome`, `Starter`, `StdioClient`, `_ChannelClient`, `finish_answer`). The comment says those imports exist so existing `from ddflow.adapters.mcp import ...` sites, including the ACP client that shared this plumbing, keep resolving. `from ddflow.adapters.mcp import send_line` therefore raises `ImportError` after this change; it succeeded before, and `_ChannelClient._send` was the caller of that helper.","digest":"816aa0d0f645636c","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp.py:329","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp.py:329"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`StdioClient.connect` assigns `self._channel = self._starter(...)` without closing an existing channel. A second `connect` (retry after timeout, or a caller that reconnects) drops the first `Channel` with no `close()`, so that server process keeps running; later `close()` only stops the replacement.","digest":"e173a182b4dd8689","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:153","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:153"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"After a successful `initialize`, `notifications/initialized` is sent with raw `json.dumps`, while every request in `_exchange` is sent with `encode` (the wire framing this module is not supposed to reimplement). A newline- or content-length-framed server therefore never sees a complete initialized frame: the next `tools/list` line is glued to the notification, the handshake never finishes, and `list_tools` returns `TIMEOUT` even though `initialize` already succeeded.","digest":"d6fceea023a83207","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:167","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:167"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":20416,"diff_sha":"6f12d15db3e31e711921d4655879cac3f17881cba7efa39b58906e64c0374e04","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":128.9,"family":"google","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"b8d4bc366fe964cc","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T124904Z-203d4298.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"6107a3eca828b080fd63a74cd8eaed6a006d279a","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/adapters/mcp.py":"100644 a3598a6870f0292a63b773cf9b3dd9cdbc6e7714","ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py":"100644 ece8f398abfea27fa53ba6e8a61c65e976a8efe2","ddflow/services/archifaces.py":"100644 b3677f76b30476e457c6087fa1a378eac87f062c"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:41","ddflow/adapters/mcp.py:329","ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:153","ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:167"],"tree_sha":"6107a3eca828+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"e1d4fd1ebd57839db6dc8a90d","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":174008,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib","ts":"2026-11-11T12:51:14.917700Z"}
