{"agent":"i1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`connect` assigns `self._channel = self._starter(...)` without closing an existing channel. A second `connect` (retry after `TIMEOUT`/`EOF`, or a caller that reconnects) drops the only reference to the first `Channel` and never calls `close`, so the first server process keeps running. `close` is the only method that stops a server, and nothing else in this module retains that channel.","digest":"e1cd905834743b1a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The initialized notification is the only outbound frame not passed through `encode`. `_exchange` sends `encode(frame)` (the line framing this module says lives in `encode`); `connect` sends `json.dumps({... notifications/initialized ...})` with no delimiter. On a newline-delimited MCP stdio channel whose `send` writes the string as given, that notification is glued to the next `tools/list`/`tools/call` line, so the server never completes `notifications/initialized` and cannot parse the following request; `list_tools` then returns `TIMEOUT` (or `ECHOED`) even though initialize succeeded.","digest":"8ae6c4c780cdc882","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":20416,"diff_sha":"6f12d15db3e31e711921d4655879cac3f17881cba7efa39b58906e64c0374e04","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":147.8,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"3295e79168b62936","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib.critic.grok-4.7.20261111T125119Z-f79fa941.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"6107a3eca828b080fd63a74cd8eaed6a006d279a","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/adapters/mcp.py":"100644 a3598a6870f0292a63b773cf9b3dd9cdbc6e7714","ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py":"100644 ece8f398abfea27fa53ba6e8a61c65e976a8efe2","ddflow/services/archifaces.py":"100644 b3677f76b30476e457c6087fa1a378eac87f062c"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect","ddflow/adapters/mcp_client.py:StdioClient.connect"],"tree_sha":"6107a3eca828+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e1bf55b4879a18183d70360ed","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":174027,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-adapters-mcp-over-20kib","ts":"2026-11-11T12:53:48.015468Z"}
